      "body": "## Motivation\n\n`EmbeddingReqInput(input_ids=[]).normalize_batch_and_arguments()` indexes `input_ids[0]` and raises `IndexError`. Reject the empty token list with `ValueError` before indexing so it follows the native encode/classify handlers' existing validation-error path.\n\nThis is specific to native request normalization; the OpenAI embeddings entry point already has its own empty-input validation.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Add an empty-list guard to `EmbeddingReqInput` only.\n- Cover the empty input and preserve both nonempty single-request and batched token inputs in the existing registered test file.\n- Use the documented `maybe_stub_sgl_kernel()` test helper before production imports, allowing this CPU test file to run without the optional kernel extension.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nRan the complete registered `test/registered/unit/managers/test_io_struct.py` file with Python 3.12 / Torch 2.11.0+cu130, CUDA hidden, and the selected source import path/hash verified:\n\n- Candidate: 66 tests run, 64 passed, 2 existing CUDA-only skips.\n- Same tests against unchanged base production code: the new empty-input test errors with `IndexError`; the other results are unchanged.\n- Focused pre-commit hooks passed on both changed files. Registered-test, no-package-registration and no-bare-pytest-main lint checks passed on the materialized managers checkout.\n\nThis is CPU request-normalization coverage, not a GPU, model or end-to-end HTTP server run. Optional-backend warnings occurred in both arms; this does not claim warning-free execution or official CI.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot applicable: input validation only; no inference-speed claim.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format changed files with pre-commit.\n- [x] Add regression coverage in the existing registered unit tests.\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style guidance.\n- Documentation and model accuracy/speed benchmarks: not applicable.\n\nAI-assisted implementation and validation; submitted and signed off by Xucheng Zhou.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38634903022](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38634903022)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38634902864](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38634902864)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38634902945](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38634902945)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
